fno-agents a2a: no TTY to confirm autonomous relay; applying the conservative fallback (autonomous relay OFF, single observed hop). Run `fno config set config.agents.a2a.auto true` to opt in.
mail-inject: not-injectable means no roster entry, or no control socket to write into. It is NOT a liveness verdict: the session may be alive and mid-turn. Ask `fno agents truth <handle>` for reachability. A session with no injection path can still act: its operator can type the command at its prompt.
mail: liveness of worker-1 could not be established; queued durably as recovery only - the recipient must drain its inbox to read this, and may never do so
  live delivery NOT confirmed - do not wait for a reply, recover:
    fno agents peek worker-1     # did it land? a busy peer may have queued it
    fno agents resume worker-1   # wakes it (claude) or resumes it (other harnesses), then re-send
    fno agents attach worker-1   # drive it yourself (claude)
    fno agents mail withdraw <id>      # none of the above? retract it